1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,133
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:35,433
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:41,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,300
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:45,433
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:46,667
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:48,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,700
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,133
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:56,200
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:58,067
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,067 --> 00:01:00,533
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,400
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,233
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,233 --> 00:01:13,633
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,633 --> 00:01:15,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:22,200
<i>These are the people
connected to the Zafras.</i>

21
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,833
<i> Let's arrest them all.</i>

22
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:25,733
<i> Who ate this?</i>

23
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:27,133
<i>Drinking water fills me up
already.</i>

24
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:28,533
<i> How dare you lie to me!</i>

25
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:31,000
<i> You lowlifes! Pigs!</i>

26
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,300
<i>We got a pedicab
from the dumpsite.</i>

27
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,567
<i> It's a bit damaged.</i>

28
00:01:34,567 --> 00:01:36,400
<i>Please fix it
so Gloria can use it.</i>

29
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,300
<i> Rudy and I got this.</i>

30
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,367
<i> I wonder how Gabo is doing.</i>

31
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,200
<i>I'm sure he has a surprise
for you when he comes home.</i>

32
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:46,933
<i>That's the vehicle you'll use
in your next mission, Gabo.</i>

33
00:01:46,933 --> 00:01:49,500
<i>- I feel like James Bond!
- Good morning, Gabo!</i>

34
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,500
<i>If you need anything,
just tell ALEX.</i>

35
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,033
<i> That's your first target.</i>

36
00:01:54,033 --> 00:01:57,467
<i>They're all connected to one
person named Misty Manalo.</i>

37
00:01:57,467 --> 00:02:00,367
<i> Misty gets around by taxi.</i>

38
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:01,867
<i>And that's where
you come in, Gabo.</i>

39
00:02:01,867 --> 00:02:04,667
<i> You are the fist of Anino.</i>

40
00:02:06,033 --> 00:02:07,867
There's no need to confront her.
It's my fault anyway.

41
00:02:07,867 --> 00:02:11,633
Yes, it's your fault, but she
shouldn't have insulted you.

42
00:02:11,633 --> 00:02:15,100
Mameng, Dante.
What are you two doing?

43
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:17,933
I'm just stopping her
from starting a fight.

44
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:21,200
Well, Dante here ate Betchay's
canned goods,

45
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:24,067
and that woman said
hurtful words.

46
00:02:24,767 --> 00:02:26,667
Seriously, Dante?

47
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:29,300
You know how Betchay is,
right?

48
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:31,233
She makes a big deal
out of small things.

49
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:32,367
What's with you, huh?

50
00:02:32,367 --> 00:02:35,267
You shouldn't have eaten those
imported canned goods.

51
00:02:36,067 --> 00:02:37,700
I just wanted to try it.

52
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:40,100
Dante, next time,

53
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,500
just ask for permission.

54
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,033
I'm sure Betchay will
give you some.

55
00:02:45,033 --> 00:02:47,033
[MAMENG] Yeah, right.

56
00:02:47,033 --> 00:02:50,633
That selfish Betchay
being generous?

57
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:53,933
- Babe. Babe.
- That's impossible!

58
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:56,100
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,067
Are you talking about me?

60
00:02:58,067 --> 00:03:00,033
[SCOFFS] Why?

61
00:03:00,033 --> 00:03:02,067
Are there other Betchays here?

62
00:03:02,067 --> 00:03:04,133
Mameng, let it go.

63
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:05,233
No way.

64
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:08,700
Did you know this woman called
us lowlifes and pigs?

65
00:03:09,533 --> 00:03:12,200
- You said that?
- I got carried away.

66
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,533
It's true anyway.

67
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:18,433
And why are you so
upset, Mameng?

68
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:21,467
Someone stole from me
in my own house.

69
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,367
I'm the one who should
be upset.

70
00:03:23,367 --> 00:03:27,167
Well, I hate your
entire personality.

71
00:03:27,167 --> 00:03:29,333
If you're bringing food
into this house,

72
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:31,367
it should be for everyone.

73
00:03:31,367 --> 00:03:33,933
I already said that was mine!
It's mine!

74
00:03:33,933 --> 00:03:37,100
And yet, you stole it!

75
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:40,067
I'll put rat poison.
Shove it down your throat!

76
00:03:40,067 --> 00:03:41,500
Betchay, that's enough!

77
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:46,300
As for you, Dante,
ask permission first

78
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,133
before cooking
and eating it!

79
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:51,100
- Yeah, I'm not selfish.
- [RUDY] And you, Betchay...

80
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:54,467
It's just right that you
keep those canned goods.

81
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,033
They're all yours!

82
00:03:56,033 --> 00:03:58,833
Keep those so you can
stop being selfish!

83
00:03:58,833 --> 00:04:05,833
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

84
00:04:09,267 --> 00:04:11,700
I really don't get that woman.

85
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:16,000
She should've just kept those
canned goods in her underpants

86
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,200
so no one will
take it from her.

87
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:24,367
Or she should've put up her
own kitchen somewhere else.

88
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:25,800
That's enough, you two.

89
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:29,167
Can't we have peace
in this house?

90
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,900
What's with that woman?

91
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:36,033
I don't know where she got
that bad attitude.

92
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:38,633
I think it started when
she went to a salon.

93
00:04:38,633 --> 00:04:40,833
It's not like it helped her
to look beautiful.

94
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:41,867
Hmph!

95
00:04:41,867 --> 00:04:45,967
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,900
[ARNEL] What's that I saw
last night?

97
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:53,367
You made an episode
without my approval!

98
00:04:53,367 --> 00:04:56,000
Boss, it's my name on the show.

99
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,667
Can't I at least create
my own story or an episode?

100
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,933
You know what, Salvador?

101
00:05:02,933 --> 00:05:04,767
You've gotten too arrogant!

102
00:05:04,767 --> 00:05:05,833
You too!

103
00:05:06,433 --> 00:05:09,000
You're right, boss.
Boss is absolutely right.

104
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,967
Look, going after Ricardo
is our winning formula.

105
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:15,267
We aired an episode
that had nothing to do with him,

106
00:05:15,267 --> 00:05:17,867
and the ratings were so low.

107
00:05:17,867 --> 00:05:20,033
If I could erase it,

108
00:05:20,733 --> 00:05:22,200
I would.

109
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,600
But the problem is
it already aired!

110
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,733
Boss.

111
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:29,533
Jacinto threatened us.

112
00:05:30,367 --> 00:05:34,200
So you're chickening out now,
Salvador? Is that it?!

113
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,233
Boss is right again, man.

114
00:05:36,267 --> 00:05:39,167
Your episodes should always
have something to do

115
00:05:39,167 --> 00:05:42,200
with the villain in your life,
which is Gen. Jacinto.

116
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:45,600
You know, honestly,
you're the villain in my life.

117
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,167
You're getting on my nerves.

118
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,533
You two are such troublemakers!

119
00:05:50,533 --> 00:05:56,067
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:05:56,067 --> 00:05:57,467
[CHAIR THUDS]

121
00:05:57,467 --> 00:05:59,033
You're unbelievable, Oli.

122
00:05:59,033 --> 00:06:01,633
You're the one who said
not to feature Jacinto,

123
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:03,800
and now you're throwing me
under the bus!

124
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,300
No, wait, man.

125
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,800
I was just making a suggestion.

126
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,900
Didn't you say you're the face
and name of the show?

127
00:06:09,933 --> 00:06:11,700
So you still have
the final say, right?

128
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:14,100
You're really getting
on my nerves.

129
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:15,600
What do you want me to do?

130
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,733
Tell the boss it was my idea?

131
00:06:17,733 --> 00:06:19,200
It was a flop, wasn't it?

132
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,467
Come on, man.

133
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:24,067
I don't want to lose my job!
I love my job!

134
00:06:24,067 --> 00:06:25,233
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

135
00:06:25,233 --> 00:06:26,667
What about me, huh?

136
00:06:26,667 --> 00:06:29,100
Did you even think of me?

137
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,333
[CARLOTTA] Lorenzo.

138
00:06:34,333 --> 00:06:35,400
Secretary.

139
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:38,133
<i>I need an update
on Project Anino.</i>

140
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:40,700
<i>With everything happening
in our country,</i>

141
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,333
<i> we need to take action.</i>

142
00:06:42,367 --> 00:06:43,800
Is your man ready?

143
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:45,333
Yes, Secretary.

144
00:06:45,333 --> 00:06:47,067
I've been training someone.

145
00:06:47,067 --> 00:06:49,800
I've seen more than
just strength in him.

146
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,500
He also has principles.

147
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,900
<i>No matter how many times
he gets knocked down,</i>

148
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:57,733
he never forgets who he is

149
00:06:57,733 --> 00:07:00,867
or who he's fighting for.

150
00:07:03,133 --> 00:07:05,700
You promised me
you'd sharpen his skills.

151
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,867
<i> Is he ready for your tests?</i>

152
00:07:08,233 --> 00:07:10,400
I've been preparing him
for a long time.

153
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:14,200
Now I'm ready to
put him to the test.

154
00:07:14,833 --> 00:07:20,633
<i>Lorenzo, I trust that you
and Gabo won't let me down.</i>

155
00:07:20,633 --> 00:07:21,933
Yes, Secretary.

156
00:07:21,933 --> 00:07:23,300
<i> And Project Anino?</i>

157
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:28,167
It will remain in the shadows,
hidden from everyone's eyes.

158
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:35,100
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:07:41,967 --> 00:07:44,867
[ENGINE REVVING]

160
00:07:44,867 --> 00:07:50,867
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:53,633
[GABO]
Alex, where are we headed?

162
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:55,100
[ALEX]
<i> In Emeralds Heights, boss.</i>

163
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,533
<i> That's where Misty's house is.</i>

164
00:07:57,533 --> 00:07:59,933
<i>Just follow
the navigation screen.</i>

165
00:07:59,933 --> 00:08:02,667
Okay. I know where it is.

166
00:08:03,333 --> 00:08:06,733
[ENGINE REVVING,
TIRES SCREECHING]

167
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:13,700
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

168
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

169
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,933
[ALEX]
<i> Don't drive recklessly, Gabo.</i>

170
00:08:27,933 --> 00:08:29,100
[GABO] Why not?

171
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:30,367
I'm on a mission!

172
00:08:31,067 --> 00:08:33,567
[ALEX]
<i> Yes, but this isn't a race.</i>

173
00:08:33,567 --> 00:08:36,233
<i>It doesn't mean you can
ignore traffic laws.</i>

174
00:08:36,233 --> 00:08:43,200
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,400
[MAN] Add more here.

176
00:08:55,433 --> 00:09:02,333
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

177
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:29,467
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

178
00:09:31,567 --> 00:09:33,167
Emerald Mall!

179
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:36,333
[GABO]  I'm sorry, sir.

180
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:38,533
I already have a passenger.
I'm just waiting for them.

181
00:09:38,533 --> 00:09:41,000
Sorry? I've been
waiting here forever!

182
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:43,567
I'm really sorry, sir.

183
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:46,000
Please just take another taxi.

184
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,167
Take another taxi?!

185
00:09:47,167 --> 00:09:50,167
I'm done waiting!
Just take me to Emerald Mall!

186
00:09:50,167 --> 00:09:51,267
I'm really sorry, sir.

187
00:09:51,267 --> 00:09:52,967
My passenger
might get mad at me.

188
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,767
You taxi drivers, I swear!

189
00:09:54,767 --> 00:09:56,667
Now you're being picky
with passengers?!

190
00:09:56,667 --> 00:09:58,567
Want me to make you famous?!

191
00:09:58,567 --> 00:10:00,533
Fine, I'm going to record you!

192
00:10:01,167 --> 00:10:04,667
Sir, there's really
no need for that.

193
00:10:04,667 --> 00:10:05,767
Hello, guys.

194
00:10:06,367 --> 00:10:10,100
See this cab driver?
Here he is.

195
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:11,800
He's so picky with passengers!

196
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:14,200
Remember that face, guys!

197
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,233
Boss, it's not that
I'm picky with passengers.

198
00:10:16,233 --> 00:10:18,767
it's just that I'm
already booked.

199
00:10:18,767 --> 00:10:21,700
If you don't want me
to wreck your cab, drive!

200
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:25,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:29,767
Okay, if you really don't want
to get another cab,

202
00:10:29,767 --> 00:10:31,033
there's nothing I can do.

203
00:10:31,033 --> 00:10:34,600
- Please put on your seat belt.
- No! Forget the seat belt!

204
00:10:34,633 --> 00:10:36,433
- Just drive!
- Are you sure?

205
00:10:36,433 --> 00:10:37,467
Drive!

206
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,833
Fine. If you say so.

207
00:10:40,833 --> 00:10:42,500
Don't blame me later.

208
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,800
- [CAB ENGINE ROARING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

209
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:50,400
- [PASSENGER SCREAMING IN FEAR]
- [GABO YELLING]

210
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:57,733
What the hell?!
Ah! Ow!

211
00:10:57,733 --> 00:11:02,033
- [CAB ENGINE ROARING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

212
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,667
Drive slowly!

213
00:11:10,067 --> 00:11:11,900
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

214
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:17,200
Aah! Hey!

215
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,867
[HORNS BLARING]

216
00:11:18,867 --> 00:11:20,033
Ah!

217
00:11:21,667 --> 00:11:22,900
Ah!

218
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:26,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

219
00:11:26,567 --> 00:11:29,167
- [CAB ENGINE ROARING]
- [PASSENGER SCREAMING]

220
00:11:29,167 --> 00:11:30,667
- [BRAKES SQUEAL]
- [LOUD THUD]

221
00:11:30,733 --> 00:11:31,733
Whoa!

222
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:34,267
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [PASSENGER GRUNTING]

223
00:11:34,267 --> 00:11:35,633
[PANTING]

224
00:11:36,767 --> 00:11:38,833
- [THWACKS]
- [THUDS]

225
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,633
- [TIRES SQUEAL]
- [PHONE SHATTERS]

226
00:11:43,667 --> 00:11:45,400
That bastard.

227
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:47,133
How dare he threaten me?

228
00:11:49,133 --> 00:11:50,100
[MAN 1] Hurry up!
Load 'em up!

229
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:51,700
[MAN 2] Hey! Be careful!
Be careful!

230
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,867
[MAN 1] Be careful!

231
00:11:55,767 --> 00:11:57,267
- It's the NCIA! Run!
- [SIREN WAILING]

232
00:11:57,267 --> 00:11:59,467
This is the NCIA! Hands up!

233
00:11:59,467 --> 00:12:01,500
- Hands up!
- Wait a minute!

234
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,400
- On the ground!
- What are you doing here?!

235
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:06,133
You are under investigation!
Come with us!

236
00:12:06,133 --> 00:12:07,167
What?!

237
00:12:07,167 --> 00:12:09,267
Secure all the documents!

238
00:12:09,267 --> 00:12:11,067
I knew you were after
the documents!

239
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:13,433
- Come on!
- Bring them in!

240
00:12:13,433 --> 00:12:14,433
Move!

241
00:12:14,467 --> 00:12:17,467
[SIREN WAILING]

242
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:21,433
Ma'am, sir, this is Gener.

243
00:12:21,433 --> 00:12:22,633
He's one of our men.

244
00:12:22,633 --> 00:12:24,000
What are you doing here?

245
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,500
And why do you look like that?

246
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,133
Some of our men
were arrested.

247
00:12:28,133 --> 00:12:29,767
I was the only one who escaped.

248
00:12:29,767 --> 00:12:32,867
The NCIA raided the warehouse
in San Isidro.

249
00:12:32,867 --> 00:12:34,400
For what?

250
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:37,300
That business is legitimate,
so why?!

251
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:41,400
They think we're behind
the attack on NCIA.

252
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,767
How many were captured?

253
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:44,600
More than 20 men, sir.

254
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:48,100
Pa, Ma, we need to do
something about this.

255
00:12:48,133 --> 00:12:52,233
Make sure that none
of them squeak.

256
00:12:52,233 --> 00:12:53,267
Yes, ma'am.

257
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:56,100
- But that's not enough.
- Good news, guys!

258
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:58,800
The criminals have been caught.
They're now in our custody.

259
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:02,467
We were only able to capture
Zafras' pawns.

260
00:13:02,467 --> 00:13:05,733
But don't worry.
We'll get them soon.

261
00:13:06,933 --> 00:13:08,133
Call a press conference.

262
00:13:08,767 --> 00:13:10,700
- On it.
- Sir Seb.

263
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:13,167
A press conference?
What for?

264
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,433
To let everyone know
that we are doing something

265
00:13:15,433 --> 00:13:18,133
and that the NCIA is
making progress.

266
00:13:18,133 --> 00:13:20,133
Wouldn't that ruin our plan?

267
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:21,933
Wouldn't it be better

268
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:24,133
to not let them know
that we're on the move?

269
00:13:24,133 --> 00:13:26,500
Karen, this is part of the plan.

270
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:30,300
For sure, the Zafras are already
aware of the raid that happened.

271
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:33,700
But what I want them to know

272
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:38,267
is that we are not afraid
of what they will do to us.

273
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,800
We're the NCIA, right?

274
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,033
We're Team Alpha. [SCOFFS]

275
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:46,933
And you've got me, Sebastian,
your team leader.

276
00:13:46,933 --> 00:13:48,033
Seb!

277
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:51,167
Hm?

278
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:01,200
You arrested Zafras' men?

279
00:14:02,733 --> 00:14:04,767
- Isn't that our mission?
- [PIA HUFFS]

280
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:09,133
Don't you think
you're being reckless?

281
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,267
Did you even get approval
from the higher-ups?

282
00:14:12,267 --> 00:14:14,600
Reckless?
Why, Ma'am Pia?

283
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:16,167
Did anything bad happen?

284
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:19,600
We planned this out carefully.

285
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,667
And if you're asking
about approval...

286
00:14:22,933 --> 00:14:24,267
I approved it.

287
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:27,700
I mobilized the whole NCIA

288
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,800
with the power that I have.

289
00:14:33,967 --> 00:14:35,300
Is there a problem?

290
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:38,033
No.

291
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:43,533
I guess I'm just antsy due to
everything that's going on.

292
00:14:44,367 --> 00:14:45,233
Why is that?

293
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,267
I'm worried about

294
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,867
what the Zafras will do

295
00:14:51,867 --> 00:14:53,667
because of what we've done.

296
00:14:54,333 --> 00:14:58,267
I wish we had discussed
this first.

297
00:14:58,267 --> 00:15:02,033
You should've consulted me first
since Sir Delgado's not here.

298
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:06,033
Ma'am Pia,
this is my area of expertise.

299
00:15:06,033 --> 00:15:10,033
Isn't reviewing your forte?

300
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:14,167
So I look forward to your
stellar review of my work

301
00:15:14,167 --> 00:15:15,333
after all this.

302
00:15:15,333 --> 00:15:19,733
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

303
00:15:19,733 --> 00:15:21,100
Excuse me.
Uh, Sir Seb?

304
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,533
We're all set for
the press conference.

305
00:15:22,533 --> 00:15:23,600
Okay.

306
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:28,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:15:28,267 --> 00:15:29,900
- [SEBASTIAN] Are we ready?
- [SEQIOA] Yeah, we're good.

308
00:15:37,133 --> 00:15:38,300
- Hey, Rudy.
- Hmm?

309
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,733
I've fixed the wiring inside.
It should work now.

310
00:15:40,733 --> 00:15:42,100
- Yeah?
- Give it a try.

311
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:43,200
All right.

312
00:15:45,267 --> 00:15:46,400
[SPEAKER CHIMES]

313
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,667
- See? I told you.
- Wow, good job.

314
00:15:48,667 --> 00:15:50,133
- It's fixed.
- And it lights up now.

315
00:15:50,133 --> 00:15:51,033
- Looks great, doesn't it?
- [SAM] I'll be right back.

316
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:52,067
- All right, Gloria.
- Okay.

317
00:15:52,067 --> 00:15:53,167
[ELTON] Of course!

318
00:15:53,167 --> 00:15:55,200
- Mm.
- You can use it now.

319
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,467
- Gloria.
- Pa, Mister Elton.

320
00:15:57,467 --> 00:15:59,667
- Gloria.
- Uh, by the way...

321
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:02,900
Elton and Badong
have a great idea.

322
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:04,633
Show it to her.

323
00:16:04,633 --> 00:16:06,633
- Go on.
- Look, Gloria.

324
00:16:06,633 --> 00:16:08,733
- And... voila!
- Ta-da!

325
00:16:08,767 --> 00:16:10,667
- Wow! It looks great!
- Ta-da!

326
00:16:10,667 --> 00:16:12,133
[CHUCKLING]

327
00:16:12,133 --> 00:16:14,000
- Do you like it?
- Looks awesome!

328
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,500
Thank you, Pa.
I love it.

329
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,300
- Nice, right?
- It doesn't look sad anymore.

330
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:18,700
- [CHUCKLES]
- Wow...

331
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:21,467
[TOLITS]
It looks good as new!

332
00:16:21,467 --> 00:16:22,400
Nice!

333
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,400
- How neat.
- [ELTON] There you go, Gloria.

334
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,533
- You can use it now.
- Thank you.

335
00:16:26,533 --> 00:16:28,667
And that's not all.
There's one more surprise.

336
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:29,900
- Whoa.
- What?

337
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:31,967
- A Bluetooth speaker?
- Really?

338
00:16:31,967 --> 00:16:33,633
- Look at this.
- How bougie!

339
00:16:33,633 --> 00:16:34,933
- Where'd you get that?
- Look.

340
00:16:34,933 --> 00:16:36,267
- There.
- Wow.

341
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:38,200
- Whoa.
- It lights up?!

342
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:40,100
- Ooh...
- Won't it fall off?

343
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:41,333
You know, Gloria,

344
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:43,000
this speaker will attract people

345
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,633
and bring in more scraps
to recycle.

346
00:16:45,633 --> 00:16:47,433
- Does it work?
- It sure does!

347
00:16:47,433 --> 00:16:48,700
Look. It's on.

348
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:52,467
Could you play a song
that'll boost our energy?

349
00:16:52,467 --> 00:16:53,967
<i> Hello? Hello? Hello?</i>

350
00:16:53,967 --> 00:16:56,033
<i>All right.
Give me a beat.</i>

351
00:16:56,033 --> 00:16:59,633
[BONG] You heard him.
One, two, three, four.

352
00:16:59,633 --> 00:17:03,800
[SINGING] <i> Gloria, Gloria,
</i> Gloria, the garbage queen!

353
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,633
<i>Gloria, Gloria,
Gloria, the garbage queen!</i>

354
00:17:06,633 --> 00:17:07,800
[BONG] Sick lyrics!

355
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:11,333
[ALL SINGING] <i> Gloria, Gloria,
</i> Gloria, the garbage queen!

356
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:14,333
<i>The garbage queen
is Gloria!</i>

357
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:15,633
- Whoo!
- Let's go!

358
00:17:15,667 --> 00:17:19,200
[SINGING]<i> The sewer was cleaned;
</i> the flooding was gone

359
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,333
- [IN UNISON] <i> Gone!
</i> - She picked up the litter

360
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:23,000
<i> Goodbye to the mosquitoes!</i>

361
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:23,900
[IN UNISON]  Goodbye!

362
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:25,267
<i> She collected garbage</i>

363
00:17:25,267 --> 00:17:27,000
<i> and got rid of the rats!</i>

364
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:27,900
[IN UNISON]  The rats!

365
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,667
<i>But she couldn't
get rid of Betchay!</i>

366
00:17:30,667 --> 00:17:33,833
[LAUGHTER, CLAPPING]

367
00:17:33,833 --> 00:17:35,867
- [CHEERING]
- Come on!

368
00:17:35,867 --> 00:17:39,300
[ALL SINGING] <i> Gloria, Gloria,
</i> Gloria, the garbage queen!

369
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,467
All together now!

370
00:17:40,567 --> 00:17:43,667
[ALL SINGING] <i> Gloria, Gloria,
</i> Gloria, the garbage queen!

371
00:17:43,667 --> 00:17:47,667
<i>Gloria, Gloria, Gloria,
the garbage queen!</i>

372
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:51,700
<i>The garbage queen
is Gloria!</i>

373
00:17:51,733 --> 00:17:55,100
<i>Gloria, Gloria, Gloria,
the garbage queen!</i>

374
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:58,733
<i>The garbage queen
is Gloria!</i>

375
00:18:00,433 --> 00:18:01,567
[ENGINE HUMMING]

376
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:15,067
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

377
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:27,133
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:18:31,767 --> 00:18:33,667
[TIRES SCREECH]

379
00:18:33,667 --> 00:18:38,233
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:39,733
[ENGINE REVS]

381
00:18:39,733 --> 00:18:40,667
[THUD]

382
00:18:41,533 --> 00:18:42,800
He beat me to it!

383
00:18:44,167 --> 00:18:45,300
[ENGINE REVS]

384
00:18:48,567 --> 00:18:55,400
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

385
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:57,700
Do you think you can
get away from me?

386
00:18:58,533 --> 00:19:02,267
I'll follow you
wherever you go.

387
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:11,067
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

388
00:19:13,533 --> 00:19:14,867
[ENGINE REVS]

389
00:19:26,067 --> 00:19:27,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

390
00:19:27,233 --> 00:19:29,133
Sir?
You wanted to see me?

391
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:30,567
Please have a seat.

392
00:19:30,567 --> 00:19:31,600
Thank you, sir.

393
00:19:34,067 --> 00:19:36,433
This is in connection
with your sister.

394
00:19:38,267 --> 00:19:40,500
The NCIA was
showered with bullets

395
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:43,533
during their tribute dinner
for Agent Sam Jacinto.

396
00:19:43,533 --> 00:19:46,167
Director Delgado
is currently in the hospital.

397
00:19:46,167 --> 00:19:48,800
The NCIA is investigating
the incident,

398
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,967
their prime suspect is
none other than the Zafras.

399
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,667
The Zafras don't have
any respect.

400
00:19:55,167 --> 00:19:57,933
Look at what they've done during
my sister's tribute dinner!

401
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:01,167
Sir, has no one caught them yet?

402
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,200
Maybe the NCIA's hands are tied

403
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:06,900
and they also don't have
any evidence against the Zafras.

404
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:07,767
Sir.

405
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,800
If we let the Zafras
get away with it,

406
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,367
they'll just become
even braver.

407
00:20:11,367 --> 00:20:15,067
Don't you think it's time
for us to fight back?

408
00:20:15,067 --> 00:20:16,667
Both the NLEA and the NCIA.

409
00:20:16,667 --> 00:20:18,367
[DOOR CLICKS OPEN, CLOSES]

410
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:20,567
I'm sorry for interrupting, sir.

411
00:20:20,567 --> 00:20:21,633
Yes?

412
00:20:21,633 --> 00:20:23,100
The NCIA has a press conference.

413
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,033
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

414
00:20:25,033 --> 00:20:26,133
[SEBASTIAN] Recently,

415
00:20:26,133 --> 00:20:29,767
this agency handled
a high-profile case.

416
00:20:31,067 --> 00:20:32,400
And because of this,

417
00:20:32,633 --> 00:20:36,367
we were frequently
attacked by suspects.

418
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,533
Ma'am.

419
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:39,800
Watch this press con of NCIA.

420
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:40,967
[SEBASTIAN]  They dragged
many people into it.

421
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,533
<i> They also killed many,</i>

422
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,067
<i> but...</i>

423
00:20:45,067 --> 00:20:48,100
<i>the time has come
to make them accountable.</i>

424
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:52,267
<i>As of today, 22 people
behind the attacks</i>

425
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:53,967
have been caught
by the NCIA.

426
00:20:53,967 --> 00:20:55,833
This group
is really being crippled.

427
00:20:55,833 --> 00:20:57,467
We have already cut off one leg,

428
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:00,000
and we will go
after the other next,

429
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,633
<i>and don't be surprised
when we reach</i>

430
00:21:02,633 --> 00:21:04,800
<i> the head of this syndicate</i>

431
00:21:05,067 --> 00:21:08,067
because we won't hesitate
to cut it off.

432
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:11,167
<i> NCIA was under attack.</i>

433
00:21:12,233 --> 00:21:15,233
<i> Team Alpha will fight back.</i>

434
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,800
Now that's how you do it.

435
00:21:17,167 --> 00:21:18,400
Immediate action.

436
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,567
Those people from the NCIA
are really arrogant.

437
00:21:20,567 --> 00:21:21,767
They're so boastfull.

438
00:21:21,967 --> 00:21:24,133
Especially him, his name is...

439
00:21:24,133 --> 00:21:25,467
Sebastian Tuazon

440
00:21:26,567 --> 00:21:28,067
He courted Sam.

441
00:21:28,567 --> 00:21:30,533
That's why he's so mad
at the Zafras

442
00:21:31,133 --> 00:21:35,200
Imagine 22 arrests in one day.
That's insane!

443
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,800
They just caught
all of Zafras henchmen.

444
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:41,567
I'll be amazed if they catch
the Zafras themselves.

445
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,467
[DOMINGO] We
should catch them, Lieutenant.

446
00:21:43,467 --> 00:21:45,833
We should be able the ones
who should catch the Zafras.

447
00:21:45,833 --> 00:21:48,700
General Jacinto
has confidence in us.

448
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:52,467
And also to show
the NCIA that the NLEA

449
00:21:52,467 --> 00:21:55,533
is not some small-time agency.

450
00:21:55,533 --> 00:21:58,367
But what if
they come after us, sir?

451
00:21:58,367 --> 00:22:00,267
[SCOFFS] I'd like
to see them try.

452
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:02,567
We'll be ready for them.

453
00:22:02,567 --> 00:22:07,733
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

454
00:22:07,733 --> 00:22:08,600
No!

455
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,533
They can't do that!

456
00:22:11,167 --> 00:22:12,567
Not to us.

457
00:22:13,433 --> 00:22:14,867
They can't go against us.

458
00:22:15,833 --> 00:22:17,367
Let's shoot them all down.

459
00:22:17,367 --> 00:22:18,700
This time,
we won't leave anyone alive.

460
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:20,500
Let's wipe out
their whole bloodline, ma.

461
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:22,267
[CHUCKLES]

462
00:22:23,733 --> 00:22:28,900
I knew it, gunning down
the NCIA was a mistake.

463
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:31,100
Whose great idea
was that anyway?

464
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,767
I gave them the green light,

465
00:22:33,767 --> 00:22:36,900
but don't act like you
don't know anything about it!

466
00:22:38,033 --> 00:22:39,233
[SIGHS] The question is,

467
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:42,367
how did they find our people?

468
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:44,533
Who ratted on us?

469
00:22:44,533 --> 00:22:45,500
Who else?

470
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:47,700
It was none other than Pia.

471
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,067
[LUCAS] It was her, papa.

472
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:50,700
She's the only one
who's pissed at us

473
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:53,600
because she thinks we included
her in the shootout.

474
00:22:53,600 --> 00:23:00,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

475
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:03,667
[LINE RINGING]

476
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:05,400
Arturo, where are you?

477
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:08,400
[ARTURO] <i> I'm here at the NCIA
</i> keeping an eye on Pia

478
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:10,000
<i> Do you need to talk to her?</i>

479
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,700
Bring her here.

480
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,600
Seb.

481
00:23:22,733 --> 00:23:24,533
- Good job.
- Thank you.

482
00:23:24,933 --> 00:23:26,133
Kudos to us.

483
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:28,767
But you just pissed
the Zafras even more.

484
00:23:28,767 --> 00:23:30,033
Well that's good.

485
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:31,200
Go ahead.

486
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:32,833
Get pissed off.

487
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:33,933
I don't care.

488
00:23:34,167 --> 00:23:35,633
What if they retaliate?

489
00:23:35,633 --> 00:23:37,000
Then they should go ahead.

490
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,433
Tell me, how?

491
00:23:38,433 --> 00:23:40,100
We already caught their people.

492
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:47,267
We don't know
how big the Zafra group is.

493
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:48,533
Pia

494
00:23:48,933 --> 00:23:50,200
We will find out.

495
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,167
And in no time,

496
00:23:52,933 --> 00:23:54,367
Zafras people,

497
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,233
no matter how many
of them they are,

498
00:23:56,567 --> 00:23:57,900
I will catch them.

499
00:23:58,367 --> 00:24:01,267
The same goes
for The Tiger's family.

500
00:24:01,733 --> 00:24:02,967
I'll bring them all to jail.

